WEBVTT

00:00:08,940 --> 00:00:16,940
what are your thoughts on using peptides? Not ozemic and all those ones. Some combinations I've

00:00:16,940 --> 00:00:25,340
looked at for perimenopause and this person lists five different peptides for perimenopause.

00:00:27,180 --> 00:00:35,420
Out of these right here, the only one that I would say that I would approve is the BPC 157 and the

00:00:35,420 --> 00:00:42,940
thymosin beta-4. The other ones are meant to stimulate an increased metabolic rate.

00:00:52,700 --> 00:00:59,180
You would not want to do that for cancer. There are certain peptides that if you're trying

00:00:59,180 --> 00:01:07,740
to increase metabolic rate, which can increase like the Tessa Borland helps with visceral fat

00:01:07,740 --> 00:01:14,060
loss, well, it does so by increasing metabolic rate. Well, you don't want to increase metabolic

00:01:14,060 --> 00:01:20,220
rate with a person with cancer. Now, let's say a person I don't have cancer anymore. Can I start

00:01:20,220 --> 00:01:32,540
taking these? Yes, you just have to be careful with some of these. There's not a decade's worth

00:01:32,540 --> 00:01:39,420
of studies on what this does to the human body. That's the only thing that I would caution you

00:01:39,420 --> 00:01:47,100
about it. I've read multiple books on peptide therapy. I know several of my friends and our

00:01:47,100 --> 00:01:53,420
practitioners that are doing peptide therapy. It shows some promise. It makes some physiological sense,

00:01:53,420 --> 00:02:00,620
but it also you just don't know what you're messing with. I personally would be cautious about it

00:02:01,580 --> 00:02:09,020
and go slow with anything that I would do because there could be some reports of some negative effects

00:02:09,020 --> 00:02:17,500
of those things. I would just be careful about it.

